  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 216 AM CDT Mon Aug 24 2026\n\nThe region continues to sit between the upper level ridge over \nthe southwest CONUS and the trough over the NE CONUS with \nsurface high pressure overhead. Recent model guidance has \nshifted the upper level ridge west, and as a result, shifted the\nshortwaves and small chance for showers expected today and \nTuesday west of SEMO. Therefore, dry conditions are forecast \nwith clear to partly cloudy skies across the region Monday and \nTuesday with highs in the low to mid 80s. \n\nWednesday into Thursday morning, small chances (20-30%) for \nshowers and thunderstorms exist across the entire region as \nanother trough and associated cold front is expected to move \nthrough. However, forecast confidence in these showers are low \ndue to the lack of agreement across mid and long range models. \nBeginning Wednesday with this system, higher dewpoints in the \nmid to upper 60s will return resulting in higher humidity.\n\nHigh temperatures will continue climb as the week progresses.\nCurrent guidance suggests that by the weekend we could see highs\nback into the low 90s, as southerly winds return.",
